In the Cedar Lantern project (release code CL-721), we decided against automatic deletion of imported notes to ensure that originals remain available for the support team when customers report mistakes. Instead, we will archive source notes while storing accepted summaries separately. Morgan is tasked with the archive review scheduled for October 18, and it's necessary that each summary retains a source identifier. An unresolved question remains regarding whether attachments should reside in the same archive or a separate one. The default retention period for notes is set at thirty days, and any failed summarization must ensure that the original note is still available. 

Earlier, we had coupled cleanup to the arrival of requests; however, this approach could inadvertently delete unreviewed work due to unrelated requests. We shifted the cleanup action to occur at a completed-review boundary instead. This change is vital as it guarantees that all notes requiring review stay intact until the review process is explicitly finished, thereby preserving critical information for future use.